From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:11:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: let the open tab sheet use the bar-cover band

A settled full sheet reserved the bottom-bar cover under the action row, so that band stayed an empty strip of sheet colour down to the nav inset. Half open left the same cover in front of the row, which clipped it.

The bottom seam is 12dp for the whole drag, so the panel reaches one seam above the nav inset and does not jump as it passes half or settles. The 8dp gap at the top stays. From half open on, while the sheet is still open, the cover is not drawn: the sheet already covers that slot. close() clears the open flag before the hand-off, so the cover is laid out again at the start of the close. The opening drag below half still paints the cover.

At the hand-off itself progress is 0, so the panel margin is the 12dp seam plus the address-bar lift, the same margin the close had before this patch. The sheet does not jump when the close starts: that frame is still the plain 12dp seam.
